<section class="panel" id="tab-discovery" data-name="discovery">
<h2>Target discovery: promising, under-studied, undrugged</h2>
<p class="lede">The screen starts from <strong>{{ cell.discovery.pool }}</strong> genes that are up in tumour in both CPTAC RNA (log2 fold change at least {{ cell.discovery.thresholds.min_rna_log2fc }}) and protein (at least {{ cell.discovery.thresholds.min_protein_log2fc }}) and that single-cell data tie mostly to one cell type (at least {{ (cell.discovery.thresholds.min_source_share * 100) | int }} % of the gene's tumour transcripts). Each gene is then checked for how much ccRCC literature it has (Europe PMC, counting only aliases that belong to that gene), whether a clinical drug or potent compounds already exist (Open Targets, ChEMBL), where the protein sits (UniProt), how much it is expressed in vital organs (Human Protein Atlas), and whether it follows grade, replicates in TCGA-KIRC, survives correction for tumour purity, tracks survival or is a selective cell-line dependency. A gene is <strong>novel</strong> when it has no clinical-stage drug and at most {{ cell.discovery.thresholds.novel_max_ccrcc_papers }} ccRCC papers ({{ cell.discovery.novel }} genes). It is a <strong>first-in-class opportunity</strong> when it is also tractable by a small molecule or an antibody, stays at or below 50 nTPM in every vital organ, replicates in TCGA-KIRC and, for tumour and stroma genes, keeps its up-regulation at purity one ({{ kpis.fic }} genes: {% for t, n in (cell.discovery.first_in_class_by_track or {}).items() %}{{ n }} {{ t }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}). These are hypotheses ranked by data, not validated targets.</p>
{% for p in f.narrative.sections.discovery or [] %}
<p class="claim" data-evidence="{{ p.evidence_ids | evattr }}">{{ p.text }} {{ p.evidence_ids | cite | safe }}</p>
{% endfor %}
<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.by_track.tumor }}</b><span>tumor-cell track</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.by_track.stroma }}</b><span>stroma / vasculature track</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.by_track.immune }}</b><span>immune track</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.novel }}</b><span>novel (no drug, little literature)</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.by_status["novel, off-tumor risk (vital-organ expression)"] or 0 }}</b><span>novel but expressed in vital organs</span></div>
</div>
{% if cell.discovery.m13 %}<div class="kpis">
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.m13.replicated }}</b><span>replicate in TCGA-KIRC (of {{ cell.discovery.pool }})</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.m13.purity_robust }}</b><span>purity-robust up-regulation</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.m13.infiltration_driven }}</b><span>immune genes that vanish at purity 1 (infiltration-driven)</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.m13.adverse_prognosis }}</b><span>higher expression, worse survival</span></div>
  <div class="kpi"><b>{{ cell.discovery.m13.selective_dependency }}</b><span>selective DepMap dependency</span></div>
</div>{% endif %}
<div class="grid two">
  {{ plot('discovery_scatter', figs.discovery_scatter) }}{{ plot('discovery_bars', figs.discovery_bars) }}
</div>
<h3>Spotlight: novel, tractable candidates</h3>
<p class="small">These are the best candidates of each track (ranked inside the track) with no clinical-stage drug, few ccRCC papers and a small-molecule or antibody route, whatever their other flags. "Off-tumor risk" means expression above 50 nTPM in a vital organ. "Not replicated" and "not purity-robust" mean the gene failed one of those two tests. Most novel tumour-cell genes are expressed in some vital organ, which is why only a few reach first-in-class.</p>
<div class="grid">
{% for r in cell.discovery_cards %}
<div class="card cand claim" data-evidence="{{ r.evidence_ids | evattr }}">
  <h3>{{ r.gene }} <span class="small">{{ r.name or "" }}</span></h3>
  <div class="meta"><span class="tag {{ r.track }}">{{ r.track }} #{{ r.rank_in_track }}</span>{% if r.status == "first-in-class opportunity" %}<span class="tag fic">first-in-class</span>{% else %}<span class="tag warn">{{ r.status | replace("novel, ", "") }}</span>{% endif %}
    <span class="tag">novelty {{ r.novelty }}</span>
    {% if r.replicated %}<span class="tag">TCGA ✓</span>{% endif %}{% if r.purity_robust %}<span class="tag">purity-robust</span>{% elif r.infiltration %}<span class="tag warn">infiltration-driven</span>{% endif %}
    {% if r.adverse_prognosis %}<span class="tag warn">worse survival</span>{% endif %}
    {% if r.mgd %}<span class="tag">MGD {{ r.mgd }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
  <p>{{ r.why }}. {{ r.evidence_ids | cite | safe }}</p>
</div>
{% endfor %}
</div>
{{ plot('safety', figs.safety) }}
<h3>Screen results (top 30 per track by novelty score) {{ q('discovery_table') }}</h3>
<div class="filters">
  <span class="small">Track</span>
  <button class="chip" aria-pressed="true" data-ftrack="all">all</button><button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-ftrack="tumor">tumor</button>
  <button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-ftrack="stroma">stroma</button><button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-ftrack="immune">immune</button>
  <span class="small" style="margin-left:10px">Status</span>
  <button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-fstatus="first-in-class opportunity">first-in-class</button>
  <button class="chip" aria-pressed="false" data-fstatus="novel">any novel</button>
  <input class="search" id="dsearch" type="search" placeholder="Search gene or cell type" aria-label="Search discovery table">
  <span class="small" id="dcount"></span>
</div>
<div class="tw"><table id="dtable">
<thead><tr><th>Gene</th><th>Track</th><th>Cell type (share)</th><th>Novelty</th><th>ccRCC / all papers</th><th>Clinical drugs</th><th>Tractability</th><th>Surface</th>
<th>Vital-organ max</th><th>Grade ρ</th><th>TCGA log2FC</th><th>At purity 1</th><th>MGD</th><th>Status</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{% for r in cell.discovery_rows %}
<tr class="claim" data-evidence="{{ r.evidence_ids | evattr }}" data-track="{{ r.track }}" data-status="{{ r.status }}" data-text="{{ (r.gene ~ ' ' ~ r.source_group ~ ' ' ~ (r.name or '')) | lower }}">
<td><strong>{{ r.gene }}</strong></td><td><span class="tag {{ r.track }}">{{ r.track }}</span></td>
<td>{{ r.source_group }} ({{ "%.0f" | format(r.source_share * 100) }}%)</td>
<td class="num"><span class="score" style="width:{{ (r.novelty * 50) | round(0) | int }}px"></span>{{ r.novelty }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.papers }} / {{ "{:,}".format(r.total_papers) }}</td><td>{{ r.drugs or "none" }}</td><td>{{ r.modalities or "—" }}</td>
<td>{{ "yes" if r.surface else "no" }}</td><td class="num">{% if r.vital is not none %}{{ r.vital | int }} ({{ r.vital_tissue }}){% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.grade | fmt }}</td><td class="num">{{ r.tcga | fmt }}{% if r.tcga is not none and not r.replicated %}*{% endif %}</td>
<td class="num">{{ r.pure | fmt }}{% if r.infiltration %} ↓{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ r.mgd | fmt }}</td><td>{{ r.status }}</td><td>{{ r.evidence_ids[:3] | cite | safe }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div>
<div class="note"><strong>Caveats.</strong> Literature volume is a Europe PMC title/abstract count for the gene symbol (plus specific aliases) and ccRCC terms; ambiguous or recently renamed symbols can under- or
over-count. “No clinical drug” and tractability come from Open Targets (predicted tractability, not experimental). Vital-organ expression is RNA (HPA consensus), not protein.
Cell-type attribution comes from a different cohort than CPTAC (12 donors, dissociation bias). TCGA log2FC marked * did not replicate; ↓ = immune gene whose change vanishes at purity 1.
DepMap tests dependency in cell lines grown in normoxia; no candidate here is a selective dependency, so these are targeting handles (antibody, ADC, radioligand), not genes the tumour needs.</div>
</section>

